<article class="env-lemma" id="05TP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05TP">Lemma <span data-tag="05TP">13.26.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. An object $I$ of $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$ is filtered injective if and only if there exist $a \leq b$, injective objects $I_ n$, $a \leq n \leq b$ of $\mathcal{A}$ and an isomorphism $I \cong \bigoplus _{a \leq n \leq b} I_ n$ such that $F^ pI = \bigoplus _{n \geq p} I_ n$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the fact that any injection $J \to M$ of $\mathcal{A}$ is split if $J$ is an injective object. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>